**/.ipynb_checkpoints

# Host node_modules must never enter the context: the frontend Dockerfile runs
# `npm ci` and then `COPY apps/frontend/ ./`, which would overwrite the freshly
# installed tree with the host's -- possibly built for a different platform.
#
# The **/ prefix is required. Unlike .gitignore, .dockerignore does NOT apply a
# bare pattern at every depth: `node_modules/` matches only a directory at the
# context root, so apps/frontend/node_modules was still being uploaded (a
# measured 523 MB build context).
**/node_modules
**/.next
